+## 6. Order and paired fields
+
+For Singular, the three inverse variables occupy a final `dp(3)` block. The
+other \(n-3\) variables use a square matrix order: the first two rows are
+assigned \(t\)-depth and \(z\)-site, and identity rows complete the matrix
+after omitting two columns with nonzero \(2\times2\) site determinant. Every
+first-row entry is positive, so this block is global. Custody records the
+matrix hash and omitted minor.
+
+This is the requested two-weight computational priority, but the normalized
+rows are not genuinely bihomogeneous after `beta=1`, binomial target
+subtraction, and localization. It is therefore honestly classified as a
+two-site matrix filtration/order, not a preserved mathematical bigrading.
+
+Each rational row is cleared once to a sign-normalized primitive integer
+polynomial. Singular's exact-Q stream and msolve's prime-field stream are
+written simultaneously from one term iterator. The exponent/coefficient
+stream hash, ordered labels, variable bijection, and both file hashes bind
+generator identity before reduction modulo \(p=1073741827\).
